    "problem": "It has remained unclear how unforced global temperature variability may change as the climate warms, limiting the relevance of climate model simulations run under pre-industrial conditions for understanding future climate.",
    "method": "This study uses a coupled climate model to compare unforced global temperature variability between a pre-industrial and a warmed, doubled-CO2 simulation, analyzing changes in the magnitude, geographic origins, and energy budget mechanisms to understand how such variability responds to a warmer background climate.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate how the magnitude and generating mechanisms of natural, unforced global mean surface temperature variability change as the climate warms, using evidence from climate model simulations.",
